            <ArticleTitle>Two studies pave the way for preoperative therapy in pancreatic cancer patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The delivery of chemotherapy and/or radiation in the preoperative setting (before surgical resection, instead of after it) has been hypothesized to improve both rates of margin-negative resection and survival.</AbstractText>
